        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds a Firefox note about <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> ignored for <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;tspan&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;textPath&gt;</code> elements</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Fixed in Firefox 158: <a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2072680\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzil.la/2072680</a></li>\n<li>A note rather than <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code>: Firefox is the only implementer of the <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> parameter</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617229323\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45905\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45905/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45905\">mdn/content#45905</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30804",
            "title": "Note getBBox() options ignored on tspan and textPath before Firefox 158",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T17:04:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-08T17:03:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 155 enabled support for a limited subset of <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/script/type/speculationrules\" rel=\"nofollow\">speculation rules</a> functionality, in Nightly only. From looking at <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2041381#c11\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2041381#c11</a>, it appears that</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>only <code class=\"notranslate\">prefetch</code> is supported (not prerender)</li>\n<li>with <code class=\"notranslate\">immediate</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">eagerness</code> only</li>\n<li>and only a <code class=\"notranslate\">urls</code> list, which means that the <code class=\"notranslate\">source</code> value of <code class=\"notranslate\">list</code> is also supported.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 158 added the <code class=\"notranslate\">moderate</code> eagerness value; see <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2061013\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2061013</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR aims to update the relevant support data to indicate all of this.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617214751\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45895\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45895/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45895\">mdn/content#45895</a></p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30803",
            "title": "Update speculation rules data to indicate Firefox support",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T17:07:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-08T16:39:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This drops an ancient note about a feature we now track independently and needless sentence from the other note.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These are style changes only.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Discovered in the process of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5765345519\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30801\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30801/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30801\">#30801</a>.</p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30802",
            "title": "`html.elements.progress`: drop needless Firefox notes",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T16:35:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-08T16:33:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Set partial on iOS 8 <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;progress&gt;</code>. This aligns us with caniuse's data on the subject.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://caniuse.com/progress\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://caniuse.com/progress</a></li>\n<li>I tested the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;progress&gt;</code> element in Browser Stack as far back as I could manage and it rendered in all of them. I believe caniuse is correct on this.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2427816733\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/1499\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/1499/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/1499\">web-platform-dx/web-features#1499</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30801",
            "title": "`html.elements.progress`: iOS renders indeterminate progress bars",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T16:28:34.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-08T16:27:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fx 158 enables support for <code class=\"notranslate\">ReadableStream</code> request bodies in <code class=\"notranslate\">fetch()</code> requests, in Nightly only for now. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1594633\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1594633</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The bug is a bit complex to follow, but from what I can see, both the <code class=\"notranslate\">accepts_readablestream</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">duplex</code> data points need setting to preview. Both are gated by the <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.fetch.streaming_upload</code> pref, and <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/web-apis/fetch-streaming-requests\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/web-apis/fetch-streaming-requests</a> points out that <code class=\"notranslate\">duplex: \"half\"</code> needs to be set to allow streams to be used in a request.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617201808\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45887\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45887/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45887\">mdn/content#45887</a></p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30794",
            "title": "Firefox 158 nightly supports streaming fetch() request body",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T11:30:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-08T11:15:05.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds <code class=\"notranslate\">pathLength</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;path&gt;</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;circle&gt;</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;ellipse&gt;</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;line&gt;</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;polygon&gt;</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;polyline&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;rect&gt;</code></li>\n<li>Support versions reflect actual rendering, meaning <code class=\"notranslate\">stroke-dasharray</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">stroke-dashoffset</code> scaled by <code class=\"notranslate\">pathLength</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;path&gt;</code>: Chrome 50, Firefox 6, Safari 14</li>\n<li>Other shapes: Chrome 57, Firefox 61, Safari 14</li>\n<li>Safari reflected the attribute in the DOM long before it affected rendering</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Tested in Chrome 154, Firefox 157 and Safari 27 by drawing each shape to a canvas with <code class=\"notranslate\">stroke-dasharray</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">pathLength</code> units and sampling pixels along the stroke</li>\n<li>Chrome 50, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;path&gt;</code>: <a href=\"https://crbug.com/536217\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://crbug.com/536217</a> (r373110)</li>\n<li>Chrome 57, other shapes: <a href=\"https://crbug.com/596043\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://crbug.com/596043</a>, <a href=\"https://codereview.chromium.org/2525233002\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://codereview.chromium.org/2525233002</a> (r435194)</li>\n<li>Firefox 6, <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;path&gt;</code>: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=643419\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=643419</a></li>\n<li>Firefox 61, other shapes: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1325320\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1325320</a> (the stroke-dash code checks for <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;path&gt;</code> at <code class=\"notranslate\">FIREFOX_60_0_RELEASE</code> and any shape at <code class=\"notranslate\">FIREFOX_61_0_RELEASE</code>)</li>\n<li>Safari 14: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/72401\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/b/72401</a> (r254657, January 2020, WebKit 610), scaling applied to any <code class=\"notranslate\">SVGGeometryElement</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5019644895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/mdn/issues/852/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852\">mdn/mdn#852</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30790",
            "title": "Add pathLength to SVG geometry elements",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T10:35:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-08T10:33:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 158 adds support for <code class=\"notranslate\">Notification.navigator</code> — the ability to specify a URL to navigate to once a notification is clicked.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5714299430\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30755\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30755/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30755\">#30755</a> adds <code class=\"notranslate\">api.Notification.navigate</code> (the property), but there are two more data points required:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.Notification.Notification.navigate</code> (the constructor option)</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">api.ServiceWorkerRegistration.showNotification.options_navigate_parameter</code> (the service worker <code class=\"notranslate\">showNotification()</code> option)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds both.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5617222240\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45900\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45900/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45900\">mdn/content#45900</a></p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30781",
            "title": "Add Notifications API `navigate` option",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T11:50:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-07T15:18:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">svgView()</code> fragment identifier, as in <code class=\"notranslate\">image.svg#svgView(viewBox(0,0,50,50))</code>, with its <code class=\"notranslate\">viewBox()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">preserveAspectRatio()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">transform()</code> parameters</li>\n<li>Marks <code class=\"notranslate\">transform()</code> as partial in Firefox: it’s applied around the center of the viewport, and after the view box in viewport pixels instead of user units</li>\n<li>Versions follow the parent <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;view&gt;</code> element and its other subfeatures (I think it’s safe to assume they were implemented at the same time)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Tested in Chrome 154, Firefox 157 and Safari 27 by drawing <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;img src=\"test.svg#svgView(…)\"&gt;</code> to a canvas and measuring where known shapes land</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">viewBox()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">preserveAspectRatio()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">translate()</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">transform()</code> give the same result in all three</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">transform(scale(0.5))</code> moves a square at 40,40 to 20,20 in Chrome and Safari, and to 45,45 in Firefox</li>\n<li>WPT: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-transform.html\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">svgview-transform.html</code></a> and <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-viewbox-then-transform.html\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">svgview-viewbox-then-transform.html</code></a> fail only in Firefox</li>\n<li>Firefox <code class=\"notranslate\">transform()</code> bug: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2066140\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2066140</a></li>\n<li>Firefox 15 implemented <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;view&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">svgView()</code> together: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=512525\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=512525</a></li>\n<li>Safari ignores the fragment when drawing an image to a canvas that was never inserted into the page, which is a canvas bug rather than an <code class=\"notranslate\">svgView()</code> one: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/322167\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/b/322167</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5019644895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/mdn/issues/852/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/852\">mdn/mdn#852</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30779",
            "title": "Add svgView() fragment identifier to SVG <view>",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-07T13:13:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-07T13:12:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.20.12) found new features shipping in today's Chromium Canary.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.RTCPeerConnection.cancelDiagnosticLogging_static (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5091582546149376\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5091582546149376</a>)</li>\n<li>api.RTCPeerConnection.startDiagnosticLogging_static</li>\n<li>api.RTCPeerConnection.stopDiagnosticLogging_static</li>\n<li>api.WebTransport.responseHeaders (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5194104408506368\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5194104408506368</a>)</li>\n<li>css.properties.position-visibility.anchor-valid (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136123851571200\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136123851571200</a>)</li>\n<li>css.properties.position-visibility.anchor-visible</li>\n<li>css.properties.text-decoration-inset (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5178263526834176\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5178263526834176</a>)</li>\n<li>css.properties.text-decoration-inset.auto</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30757",
            "title": "Updates for Chrome Canary, 05 Oct 2026",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-08T16:00:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-05T16:38:43.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286386?u=bc4894b945491e0834d2306dade7fef748ddf698&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The spec has been updated and new values have been added to simplify the sharing of random values.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">element-scoped</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">property-scoped</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">property-index-scoped</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">fixed &lt;number&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Used <a href=\"https://codepen.io/editor/CodeRedDigital/pen/01a10c48-2a3a-760a-b650-b5e5bc8c6dde\" rel=\"nofollow\">this pen</a> to test:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox Nightly (159.0a1) - all passed</li>\n<li>Chrome Canary (157.0.8086.0) - all passed</li>\n<li>Safari Tech Preview (252) - all passed</li>\n<li>Safari (27.0) - all passed, except <code class=\"notranslate\">property-scoped</code> &amp; <code class=\"notranslate\">property-index-scoped</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45729\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45729/hovercard\">Content PR</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45997\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45997/hovercard\">Firefox Release PR</a></li>\n</ul>",
